WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.649
India's cheetahs didn't just

2
00:00:01.649 --> 00:00:02.149
come back.

3
00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:04.119
A court had to say yes first.

4
00:00:04.619 --> 00:00:06.479
The cheetah was declared

5
00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:08.417
extinct in India in 1952.

6
00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:10.896
In January 2020, the Supreme

7
00:00:10.896 --> 00:00:13.069
Court allowed African cheetahs

8
00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:15.047
to be brought to a suitable habitat.

9
00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:17.119
It called this an introduction,

10
00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:18.305
not a re-introduction,

11
00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:19.995
and set up an expert committee

12
00:00:19.995 --> 00:00:20.623
to guide it.

13
00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:22.843
The first eight came from Namibia,

14
00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:25.653
released at Kuno in September 2022.

15
00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:28.056
Twelve more came from South

16
00:00:28.056 --> 00:00:29.252
Africa in 2023.

17
00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:31.696
As of September 2026, India

18
00:00:31.696 --> 00:00:33.513
has over fifty cheetahs,

19
00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:35.064
most of them born here.

20
00:00:35.514 --> 00:00:36.922
Permission came first.

21
00:00:37.122 --> 00:00:38.487
The work came after.

22
00:00:38.987 --> 00:00:39.883
Your turn.

23
00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:41.503
Where did the first cheetahs

24
00:00:41.503 --> 00:00:41.975
come from?
